  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Esbriet (pirfenidone) Criteria Version 1: Original 3/1/21; Approval 4/16/2021; Effective 5/24/2021.",
    "Encoded: closed IPF indication, approval criteria 1–8 and denial criteria 2–3. Denial criterion 1 (failure to meet approval criteria) is represented by the approval clauses. Clinical documentation attestations require manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor ALT, AST and bilirubin and drug-induced liver injury. Gastrointestinal disorders have been observed. Photosensitivity and rash have been noted; avoid sunlight and sunlamps and wear sunscreen and protective clothing daily.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months with documentation showing improvement and effectiveness of therapy.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): 180 × 267 mg capsules per 30 days; 90 × 801 mg capsules per 30 days. Numeric quantity enforcement is not encoded.",
    "Documentation verification, monitoring, duration, reauthorization response and quantity limits require manual review. Ofev is linked as an alternative subject to its own criteria; its pack is partially encoded and requires its own eligibility review."
  ],
